SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later

SignPath doesn't read this file. It is a copy, kept here for review, of the artifact configuration entered in
the SignPath project under the slug "installer", which .github/workflows/release.yml names when it sends
TapewrightSetup.exe; change the two together. upload-artifact zips what it uploads, so the root is a
zip-file. SignPath Foundation requires the product name to be the project's and one product version per
build, so only a TapewrightSetup.exe that says Tapewright and the version release.yml passes is signed.
-->
<artifact-configuration xmlns="http://signpath.io/artifact-configuration/v1">
  <parameters>
    <parameter name="version" required="true" />
  </parameters>
  <zip-file>
    <pe-file path="TapewrightSetup.exe" product-name="Tapewright" product-version="${version}">
      <authenticode-sign />
    </pe-file>
  </zip-file>
</artifact-configuration>
